    notes: "UNCHANGED - pre-existing tag from before this project, not touched this session | Re-verified 2026-08-20: figures confirmed current and accurate, no change needed. | PART 5 PRIMARY-TEXT READ 2026-08-27 (Taylor supplied full C.R.S. 38-12-503): MATERIAL CORRECTION. Prior clause ended with 'If a repair will reasonably take longer than 60 consecutive days to complete, Landlord will notify Tenant in writing of the expected timeline' - no such duty exists in 38-12-503. The statute's 60-day figure is the hotel-room cap in (4)(c) and was misattributed. Replaced with the duties that DO exist: 24-hour contact with intentions and estimate (6)(a)(I); duty to inform tenant of the relocation obligation (6)(a)(II); 24-hour advance written entry notice for remedial action (6)(a)(III). Also corrected the 72-hour trigger to track the statute ('uninhabitable as described in 38-12-505 or otherwise') rather than 'any other condition Landlord is responsible to repair under this Lease.' Not stated in the clause but relevant to landlord risk: rebuttable presumptions of failure attach at 7 days (life/health/safety) and 14 days (uninhabitable) under (3)(a)(II).",
