    notes: "NEW | AUDIT 2026-08-27 (Opus/high/research re-audit): FEDERAL CURRENCY FLAG - HUD withdrew FHEO-2020-01 (the assistance-animal guidance) effective 2025-09-17 (Fed. Reg. Docket FR-6571-N-01); HUD states it 'should not be relied upon.' The clause text does not cite FHEO-2020-01 and rests on the Fair Housing Act itself (42 U.S.C. 3601 et seq.; 24 CFR 100.204), which is unchanged - so the operative language still stands. Flagged NEEDS_REVIEW rather than corrected because the federal posture is in flux (including post-Loper Bright litigation over the ESA no-fee rule) and any HUD replacement guidance should be picked up. CO-specific layer (documentation limits, misrepresentation warning) is unaffected. | ESA/FEDERAL-DIVERGENCE RESOLUTION 2026-08-27: RESOLVED to VERIFIED. Ran down whether the CO clause was leaning on federal law for the ESA piece - it is not. C.R.S. 24-34-502 (CADA) independently makes it a discriminatory housing practice to refuse a reasonable accommodation necessary for a person with a disability to use and enjoy a dwelling, and that covers assistance animals including ESAs; HB 21-1271 layers the documentation limits and misrepresentation penalties already captured in this clause. None of that depends on HUD guidance, so HUD's 2025 withdrawal and its May 22 2026 enforcement memo do not disturb the Colorado basis. Clause text UNCHANGED. Source caveat: much of the available commentary is ESA-certification-industry material with a commercial interest in broad ESA protection and was discounted; reliance is on the CADA statutory structure plus Colorado practitioner commentary. One source cited C.R.S. 24-34-803 as a housing-specific assistance-animal provision - NOT confirmed, not relied on, flagged for the next CO review. | MATERIAL CORRECTION 2026-08-28 (citation-existence screen, Tier 1): bodyText said misrepresentation 'is a criminal offense'. INACCURATE for 18-13-107.3, the HOUSING-relevant section, which CO reclassified as a CIVIL INFRACTION (2024/2025 CRS text: 'commits a civil infraction'). Only 18-13-107.7 (service animals, public accommodations) remains a petty offense. Changed to 'is unlawful under', accurate for both. Both citations CONFIRMED TO EXIST (added by HB 16-1426, eff. 2017-01-01). 'Escalating fines' VERIFIED: $25 / $50-200 / $100-500. RETAINED as correct: 'as required for enforcement under Colorado law' - prior warning is an ELEMENT of both offenses (107.3(1)(b), 107.7(1)(b)).",
