    notes: "NEW (Part 5 read 2026-08-27) - MATERIAL OMISSION, and an unusual one. C.R.S. 38-12-503(11) grants the landlord this termination right ONLY 'if permitted by the rental agreement.' The right does not exist by default - a lease that is silent forfeits it entirely. This is the opposite of most Part 5 provisions, which constrain the landlord regardless of lease text. Passes the three-bucket test on ground 3 (and then some): omitting it costs the landlord a statutory right. All statutory conditions in (11)(a)-(f) are stated so the clause cannot be invoked improperly.",
