    notes: "NEW (audit 2026-08-27) - closes a real statutory gap. C.R.S. 38-12-701(2)'s 60-day notice applies ONLY where there is no written agreement, so a written month-to-month lease that is silent on rent-increase notice has no statutory default. Stating a period in the lease removes the ambiguity. The 38-12-702 once-per-12-months cap applies regardless and is restated here because it constrains the landlord's own term.",
